# Contributing Templated Code

This project was created with the [ABLE Workflow Copier]({% raw %}{{ able_workflow_copier_docs }}{% endraw %}) template.

??? note "Audience: Project Contributors"

    This section is for project contributors updating files that were originally
    generated by one of the ABLE workflow copier templates.

    If you just ran copier and are implementing a new scaffold for the first time,
    start with the relevant post-copy checklist instead.

Each of the pages in this section provides information on each template applied and how to update it. You can also see the "answers" used to apply each template in the `.copier-answers/` directory. DO NOT EDIT THESE FILES MANUALLY.

## How the copier repositories fit together

New ETL steps are usually created by applying copier templates in layers:

1. `able-workflow-copier` creates the project-level scaffold.
2. `able-workflow-module-copier` adds dataset/feature/model module scaffolding.
3. `able-workflow-etl-copier` adds an ETL process under a selected module.
4. `able-workflow-rule-copier` can add standalone rules that are not ETL-based.

This layered approach keeps project structure consistent and reduces hand-edited
boilerplate.

## Generating templated code

### New Module (e.g., group of related ETL steps)

Generate templated code for a new module (e.g., under `datasets/`, `features/`, or `models/`) with the following command:

```bash
conda activate {{ package_name }}-py312-dev
copier copy --trust {% raw %}{{ able_workflow_module_copier_repo }}{% endraw %}.git ./
```

For more details, see the full [`able-workflow-module-copier` documentation]({% raw %}{{ able_workflow_module_copier_docs }}{% endraw %})

### New ETL step within an existing module

Generate templated code for a new ETL step under an existing module with the following command:

```bash
conda activate {{ package_name }}-py312-dev
copier copy --trust {% raw %}{{ able_workflow_etl_copier_repo }}{% endraw %}.git ./
```

For more details, see the full [`able-workflow-etl-copier` documentation]({% raw %}{{ able_workflow_etl_copier_docs }}{% endraw %})

### New standalone rule that is not part of an ETL process

Generate templated code for a new standalone Snakemake rule with the following command:

```bash
conda activate {{ package_name }}-py312-dev
copier copy --trust {% raw %}{{ able_workflow_rule_copier_repo }}{% endraw %}.git ./
```

For more details, see the full [`able-workflow-rule-copier` documentation]({% raw %}{{ able_workflow_rule_copier_docs }}{% endraw %})

## Updating

Update the project with changes to any of the ABLE Workflow Copier templates by running the following, where `<COPIER_ANSWERS_FILE>.yml` is the answers file for the template you want to update (e.g., `.copier-answers/project.yml` for the main project template):

```bash
conda activate {{ package_name }}-py312-dev
copier update --trust --answers-file ".copier-answers/<COPIER_ANSWERS_FILE>.yml"
```
